# Walkthrough - Role Alignment & Onboarding Finalized

I have successfully aligned the application with its intended user role architecture and integrated the onboarding flow.

## 1. Database Logic Alignment
I refactored the invitation acceptance logic to use the authoritative `users` table instead of the deprecated `user_roles` table. The logic now uses `.update()` to supplement existing records created by the Supabase trigger.

**Verified in [InvitationWelcomeScreen.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/InvitationWelcomeScreen.tsx):**
```typescript
const handleJoin = async () => {
    // ... logic to update users table
    const { error } = await supabase
        .from('users')
        .update({ 
            role: role.toLowerCase(),
            organization_name: schoolName,
            onboarding_completed: true,
            onboarding_completed_at: new Date().toISOString()
        })
        .eq('id', session.user.id);
    // ... redirect to Main
};
```

## 2. Onboarding Flow Integration
Authenticated users who have not yet completed their onboarding are now automatically directed to the [OnboardingScreen](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/OnboardingScreen.tsx#43-431).

**Integrated in [App.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/App.tsx):**
```tsx
{!session ? (
  <AuthScreen />
) : !onboardingCompleted ? (
  <OnboardingScreen onComplete={() => useStore.getState().setOnboardingCompleted(true)} />
) : (
  <TabNavigator ... />
)}
```

